docs {
  # GET /quiz-attempt-details/{id}
  
  Retrieves attempt records for a quiz.
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `GET`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/quiz-attempt-details/:id`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **Requires** API key + Bearer JWT.
  - Students see only their own attempts; instructors/admins with course access see all.
  - **Required Permission:** `Read`, `Read/Write`, or `All`
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `id` | `integer` | **Yes** | Quiz post ID. |
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK (Success)
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_quiz",
    "message": "Quiz attempts retrieved successfully",
    "data": [
      {
        "attempt_id": "88",
        "user_id": "14",
        "total_questions": "10",
        "total_answered_questions": "10",
        "total_marks": "100.00",
        "earned_marks": "90.00",
        "attempt_status": "attempt_ended",
        "attempt_info": {},
        "attempt_started_at": "2026-02-01 14:20:00",
        "attempt_ended_at": "2026-02-01 14:45:00",
        "is_manually_reviewed": "0",
        "manually_reviewed_at": null,
        "attempts_answer": []
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  Attempt rows do not include `course_id` / `quiz_id` in the SQL select. Nested answers are under `attempts_answer`; `is_correct` may be hidden for students.
  
  ### 404 Not Found
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_quiz",
    "message": "Quiz attempts not found for given ID",
    "data": []
  }
  ```
}
